MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "A Musical Affair feels like a natural next choice because I already listened to the live Japan release and want to explore another recording of that music.",
    "To Be Loved and Nostalgia appeal to my interest in expressive vocals and familiar standards, while Blown Away connects with the country listening reflected in 747 and Golden."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Christmas albums connect with something I have listened to before, but I want everyday listening now; the seasonal theme is the reason I would pass.",
    "Summer Forever feels less connected to the orchestral music and expressive vocals I want today, and I do not recognize enough about Lifer to expect a close match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing desire for more holiday albums.",
    "A broad connection to my country listening is not enough by itself; Blown Away feels relevant, but Summer Forever does not give me the same reason to choose it today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice was relaxing classical music, which adds a reason to consider orchestral and calmer listening alongside vocal albums.",
    "The connection between A Musical Affair and the live Japan recording matters more to me than a general resemblance to something I once played."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices understood my interest in melodic vocals and some country music, but placed too much weight on past Christmas listening for what I want now."
}
